Map __ballot_sync to __ballot on HIP below ROCm 7.0.

The ROCm 6.3 wheel fails to compile topk-moe.cu:118 with "use of undeclared
identifier '__ballot_sync'". The grouped-experts code from llama.cpp #29181 is
guarded by HIP_VERSION >= 60300000. ROCm declares the *_sync warp builtins by
default only from 7.0, and hip.h mapped every other *_sync but not this one.

Backport of upstream 78febbad9d (llama.cpp #31259), one day after b11960.
Not a ggml-* patch: whisper.cpp v1.9.4 calls __ballot_sync only in fattn.cu,
which excludes HIP. Delete at the next llama.cpp bump.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vendors/hip.h b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vendors/hip.h
index 8e8f5a4..61769f4 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vendors/hip.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vendors/hip.h
@@ -254,6 +254,10 @@ typedef __hip_fp8_e4m3 __nv_fp8_e4m3;
 #define FP8_AVAILABLE
 #endif // HIP_VERSION >= 60300000
 
+#if HIP_VERSION < 70000000
+#define __ballot_sync(mask, var) __ballot(var)
+#endif //HIP_VERSION < 70000000
+
 typedef int8_t int8x4_t __attribute__((ext_vector_type(4)));
 typedef uint8_t uint8x4_t __attribute__((ext_vector_type(4)));
 static __device__ __forceinline__ int __vsubss4(const int a, const int b) {
